    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTo see current offers or place your own offer on this property, please visit SherryFitz.ie and register for your mySherryFitz account.\n\nA most distinctive and characterful cut stone residence, which has been sensitively, with great skill and craftmanship, converted & restored from its original purpose to a wonderful private home. The result is a most charming residence, brimming with period features and architectural flourishes, and enjoying a much sought after location equidistant to Corrigeenroe and Knockvicar and adjacent to the majestic Lough Key.Featuring superb, natural stone masonry to all facades, this home enjoys a private cul-de-sac setting surrounded by woodland and situated in an area of outstanding natural beauty and outdoor amenities and activities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance porch - 2.36 x 1.81m\nwith flagstone floor, beamed ceiling, period window and Velux roof light, mahogany entrance door and original oak inner door and ironmongery\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 16.50m x 5.30m\nOpen plan living, dining, kitchen area featuring white oak flooring with a lovely patina, original stone surround windows and entrance porch. Handcrafted filled kitchen units with granite worktops and breakfast bar, Rayburn oil fired cooker, dishwasher, Bosch fridge freezer. Solid fuel stove on granite plinth with steel flue, book shelves, track lighting, feature stone brackets.Underfloor heating to this area.\n\nUtility Room - 2.34m x 2.11m\nTiled floor, vaulted ceiling and period window, track lighting, newly installed Grant Indoor oil burner, hardwood external door with glazed panel, original inner door.Handcrafted hardwood stairwell to first floor.\n\nLanding area - \n18.43m²white oak flooring, original vaulted ceiling features, radiators x2, Velux roof lights x4\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.48m x 2.72m\nwith vaulted ceiling and oak flooring, radiators x2, good natural light from Velux roof light and two windows\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.22m x 2.70m\nBuilt in wardrobes, Velux roof light, oak flooring, radiator, stairs to loft sleeping area (2.83m x 1.97m; sq ft x sq ft) with Velux roof light\n\nBathroom - 2.68m x 2.44m\noak wood flooring, wood panelling, bath with rain shower overhead, Velux roof light, downlighters, vanity basin with granite surround and undercabinet, wc and whb\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.13m x2.74m\noak flooring, built in wardrobe, Velux roof light, radiator, stairs to overhead loft sleeping area (2.78m x 2m; sq ft x sq ft) with Velux roof light\n\nJack and Jill bathroom - 3.77m x 2m\nwith dressing room area and built in wardrobe, ceramic floor tiling, shower enclose with rain shower, wc and whb, fixed wall mirror and shaver light, downlighters, radiator\n\nBedroom 4 - 5.48m x 2.59m\noak wood flooring, windows x2, radiators x2, Velux roof lights, track lighting, built in wardrobes, vaulted ceiling feature\n\nOFCH, Solid fuel stove, Oil fired Rayburn cooker - \n\n\nLarge wooden shed - 8.42m x 5.52m\nwith metal roof and ramp entrance, raised marine plywood floor, windows x4, electric power, double doors, and side doors x2.\n\nExternal - \nExtensive tarmac parking apron with dual vehicular access and lawns, mature wooded setting, totalling circa 0.5 acres.Open lean-to shed 9.12m x 2.12mWater tapExterior lighting\n\nHistory - \nKilbryan Church of Ireland was consecrated in 1856 with its church bell supplied by Thomas Hodges, Founder, of Abbey St., Dublin.An exceptionally rare opportunity to acquire a home of much character and history.\n\n"
      },
      {
